 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 505785,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Calculate the following:<br>\n<span data-math=\"1.14 \\times {10^{ - 43}} + 2.56\\,{ \\times\\, 10^{ - 46}}\">1.14 \\times {10^{ - 43}} + 2.56{ \\times ^{ - 46}}</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"1.14 \\times {10^{ - 43}} + 2.56 \\times {10^{ - 46}}\"></span></p>\n<p>First, you need the two numbers to have the same power of 10.</p>\n<p>Make them both have an exponent of –43. Move the decimal point three places to the left for the second number.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"0.00256 \\times {10^{ - 43}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Because the powers of 10 match, use the distributive property to factor the power of 10 from the numbers. Then, add the other part of the numbers separately.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"1.14 \\times {10^{ - 43}} + 0.00256 \\times {10^{ - 43}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"(1.14 + 0.00256) \\times {10^{ - 43}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"(1.14 + 0.00256) \\times {10^{ - 43}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"1.14256 \\times {10^{ - 43}}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"1.14256 \\times {10^{ - 43}}\">1.14256 \\times {10^{ - 43}}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
